<title>USA: East Baton Rouge Parish, La., approves road tax.</title>
<headline>East Baton Rouge Parish, La., approves road tax.</headline>
<dateline>BATON ROUGE, La. 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Louisiana's East Baton Rouge Parish voted to extend a half-cent sales tax for road work for five years, the Advocate reported.</p>
<p>The extension was approved by nearly 70 percent of those voting in a Saturday referendum.</p>
<p>The tax extension is expected to raise $130 million over five years, with $78 million earmarked for 10 road construction projects and the remainder allocated for repairs.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
